    "https://careers.newark.rutgers.edu/channels/graduate-students/": {
      "title": "Graduate Students",
      "description": "Graduate Students – Career Resources and Exploration | Rutgers University – Newark Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Log in Sign up Guests Search Keywords Make an Appointment Rutgers-Newark Handshake Request a Workshop Home About Us Staff CRE Student Employees Student Outcomes People We Connect Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Campus Partners Faculty Employers/Recruiters Family Industry Pathways Exploring/Multiple Interests Arts, Media, & Entertainment Data & Technology Financial Services, Logistics, & Management Government, Law, & Public Policy Healthcare, Pharmaceuticals, & Sciences Natural Resources, Sustainability, & Environmental Science Nonprofit, Social Justice, & Education Explore Opportunities Detecting Fraudulent Job Postings Experiential Opportunities Jobs and Internships Job Searching Making Connections Rutgers Scarlet Service Internship (RSSI) Program Professional Resources CareerThreads – Free Professional Attire Raider Headshot Studio Majors and Careers Get Career Ready Career Ready in Real Life Resumes and Cover Letters Interviewing Graduate and Professional School Personal Statements Videos on Demand Events All Events Fall 2026 Raider Career and Internship Fair at Rutgers University-Newark Raider Career Impact Awards Graduate Students What action will you take with your career? Small, constant progress will help you continue moving forward, no matter where you are in your career preparation. Internship Guidelines for Students at Rutgers University- Newark (RU-N) The Office of Career Resources and Exploration uses the NACE 7 point criteria to determine if an experience is an internship.  For more information on the NACE criteria for an experience to be defined as an internship visit: https://www.naceweb.org/about-us/advocacy/position-statements/position-statement-us-internships/ . Contact us at careers@newark.rutgers.edu with any questions. Consider your Strengths Reflecting on what you do well, what you like to do, and what’s important to you can help you to think about how those fit with your career choices. Resources within Rutgers-Newark Handshake : self-guided tools to help you learn more about yourself and connect that information to careers (myIDP, ImaginePhD, and Traitify) Explore your Options Learning more about careers, internships, jobs, and other opportunities can help you to know more about what you may not know exists. Experiential Opportunities Tell your Story Communicating who you are in effective ways is the best way to get the attention of recruiters and employers. Resumes and Cover Letters Interviews Deliver your Message Connecting with others and presenting your best self will help you reach your career goals. Making Connections Job and Internship Search Sidebar Latest News January is the month to reset your job search and build real momentum How college students and recent grads should use their career service offices | From Dorms to Desks Podcast | ep10 Advice for Transfer Students: Where to Find Rutgers Student Resources 5 Things You Can Do This Winter Break to Get Career Ready College Study Hacks: How To Memorize Faster, Retain More, And Do Better On Exams View All Career Resources Versatile PhD Share This: Share Versatile PhD on Facebook Share Versatile PhD on LinkedIn Share Versatile PhD on X Copy Link The Versatile PhD mission is to help graduate students, ABDs and PhDs identify, prepare for and excel in professional careers. … Read More Aurora by Beyond the Professoriate Share This: Share Aurora by Beyond the Professoriate on Facebook Share Aurora by Beyond the Professoriate on LinkedIn Share Aurora by Beyond the Professoriate on X Copy Link “AURORA is the only online professional development training platform for graduate students, postdocs, faculty, and PhDs that helps them successfully … Read More Resume Outline Example Share This: Share Resume Outline Example on Facebook Share Resume Outline Example on LinkedIn Share Resume Outline Example on X Copy Link View an example resume to help build your resume for your job search. Always remember to tailor your bullet points … Read More Recruiting Timeline and Industry Insights: Nonprofit, Social Justice & Education Share This: Share Recruiting Timeline and Industry Insights: Nonprofit, Social Justice & Education on Facebook Share Recruiting Timeline and Industry Insights: Nonprofit, Social Justice & Education on LinkedIn Share Recruiting Timeline and Industry Insights: Nonprofit, Social Justice & Education on X Copy Link Recruiting Timeline and Industry Insights\nNonprofit, Social Justice & Education Use the timelines and insights below to guide your search … Read More Recruiting Timeline and Industry Insights: Healthcare, Pharmaceuticals & Science Share This: Share Recruiting Timeline and Industry Insights: Healthcare, Pharmaceuticals & Science on Facebook Share Recruiting Timeline and Industry Insights: Healthcare, Pharmaceuticals & Science on LinkedIn Share Recruiting Timeline and Industry Insights: Healthcare, Pharmaceuticals & Science on X Copy Link Recruiting Timeline and Industry Insights\nHealthcare, Pharmaceuticals & Science Use the timelines and insights below to guide your search for … Read More Recruiting Timeline and Industry Insights: Government, Law & Public Policy Share This: Share Recruiting Timeline and Industry Insights: Government, Law & Public Policy on Facebook Share Recruiting Timeline and Industry Insights: Government, Law & Public Policy on LinkedIn Share Recruiting Timeline and Industry Insights: Government, Law & Public Policy on X Copy Link Recruiting Timeline and Industry Insights\nGovernment, Law & Public Policy Use the timelines and insights below to guide your search … Read More View All Resources Fellowships A fellowship is a way for students, typically graduate or doctoral students, to get funding to support their education and training. They are available for a range of academic areas and organizations, and often involve an application process in order for students to be selected based on certain criteria. See below for fellowships that you can apply for today! JPG Enterprises View All Jobs Capital Fellows Programs View All Jobs Neuhaus Education Center View All Jobs Grace Bible Church View All Jobs Foster Success View All Jobs Rich Earth Institute View All Jobs View More Videos Career.io Career Pathways Video post Interviewing mistakes Veterans Should Avoid When Interviewing for Civilian Positions (Part 1 of 9) Video post How to successfully ask for a raise at work Video post Practical Steps to Find Employment After Prison Video post International Students: Visa Process and Time Frame Video post Business Etiquette Part Two: Workplace and Communications Video post View All Videos Facebook Instagram X (formerly Twitter) runsa@newark.rutgers.edu CARE Team © 2026 Rutgers University - Newark  |  All Rights Reserved Universitywide New Brunswick Camden RBHS MyRutgers Blackboard ScarletMail People Search Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution Privacy Policy | Terms of Service"
