    "https://careers.newark.rutgers.edu/channels/campus-partners/": {
      "title": "Campus Partners",
      "description": "Campus Partners – Career Resources and Exploration | Rutgers University – Newark Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Log in Sign up Guests Search Keywords Make an Appointment Rutgers-Newark Handshake Request a Workshop Home About Us Staff CRE Student Employees Student Outcomes People We Connect Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Campus Partners Faculty Employers/Recruiters Family Industry Pathways Exploring/Multiple Interests Arts, Media, & Entertainment Data & Technology Financial Services, Logistics, & Management Government, Law, & Public Policy Healthcare, Pharmaceuticals, & Sciences Natural Resources, Sustainability, & Environmental Science Nonprofit, Social Justice, & Education Explore Opportunities Detecting Fraudulent Job Postings Experiential Opportunities Jobs and Internships Job Searching Making Connections Rutgers Scarlet Service Internship (RSSI) Program Professional Resources CareerThreads – Free Professional Attire Raider Headshot Studio Majors and Careers Get Career Ready Career Ready in Real Life Resumes and Cover Letters Interviewing Graduate and Professional School Personal Statements Videos on Demand Events All Events Fall 2026 Raider Career and Internship Fair at Rutgers University-Newark Raider Career Impact Awards Campus Partners Everyone can be a part of a student’s career journey. We welcome the opportunity to support the career readiness of your students, to collaborate with you on career related initiatives, or to discuss other opportunities to build partnerships. If you need more information on how to support students with detecting fraudulent job postings, check out the page dedicated to it. https://careers.newark.rutgers.edu/channels/detecting-fraudulent-job-postings/ Learn More About Request a Presentation by a CRE Representative Looking for a career workshop? Our workshops are interactive, with specific learning outcomes. Some of our common topics are listed below, but feel free to request others: Resumes and cover letters, Interviewing, Internship/Job Search, Networking Request a workshop by completing our request form Rutgers-Newark Handshake Rutgers-Newark Handshake is the Office of Career Resources and Exploration’s platform for sharing opportunities, resources, events, and other information with students. With Rutgers-Newark Handshake, students can: Discover career opportunities across hundreds of companies. Access personalized internship and job recommendations based on major and interests. Ask for advice from other students across the country who got great jobs (peer-to-peer features—reviews, Q & A, messaging). Share their student profile (employers can proactively contact students with public profiles; students with complete profiles are 5X more likely to be messaged by employers). The CRE has also posted career-related events and career resources within Rutgers-Newark Handshake. If you have an on-campus job you would like to share with students, you can post it in Rutgers-Newark Handshake: On-Campus Job Posting Instructions Collaborations The Office of Career Resources and Exploration can collaborate with you on career initiatives. Below are a few of the more commonly requested collaborations, and we welcome discussion of other initiatives not listed: Internships: Review internship descriptions to see that they align with the criteria set by the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE). Employer/recruiter referrals: Outreach/follow up to employers or recruiters who may be sharing opportunities with you. Career Closet: Collection of clothing for the workplace (business casual or business professional); distributed to students free of cost at several events throughout the semester. Internship Guidelines for Campus Partners: Faculty/Staff The Office of Career Resources and Exploration uses the NACE 7 point criteria to determine if an experience is an internship.  For more information on the NACE criteria for an experience to be defined as an internship visit: https://www.naceweb.org/about-us/advocacy/position-statements/position-statement-us-internships/ . Contact us at careers@newark.rutgers.edu with any questions. Sidebar Event, Presentation, and Workshop Request Interested in requesting a CRE member to speak at your event, or workshop? Want to collaborate with the CRE on an event? Let us know! Contact Us Latest News The Ultimate Guide to AI in Career Services: Helping Students Use AI Ethically and Effectively 5 Creative Ways to Engage Students with Career Services Get Free Career Coaching Exercises for Resumes, Networking, and Interviews 4 Tactics to Improve the Way Students Accept a Job Offer Supporting Non-Citizens in College Supporting Non-Citizens in College View All Career Resources Faculty Toolkit Share This: Share Faculty Toolkit on Facebook Share Faculty Toolkit on LinkedIn Share Faculty Toolkit on X Copy Link View Resource Person-Centered Language Share This: Share Person-Centered Language on Facebook Share Person-Centered Language on LinkedIn Share Person-Centered Language on X Copy Link Read the University of Minnesota’s resource on person-centered language. “Person-centered language is language that puts people first. People are so … Read More The Center for Nuleadership on Urban Solutions: An Open Letter to Our Friends on the Question of Language Share This: Share The Center for Nuleadership on Urban Solutions: An Open Letter to Our Friends on the Question of Language on Facebook Share The Center for Nuleadership on Urban Solutions: An Open Letter to Our Friends on the Question of Language on LinkedIn Share The Center for Nuleadership on Urban Solutions: An Open Letter to Our Friends on the Question of Language on X Copy Link A letter from The Center for Nuleadership on Urban Solutions on the importance of language in referring to people who … Read More Update Your Profile to Receive Alerts Tailored to your Interests! Share This: Share Update Your Profile to Receive Alerts Tailored to your Interests! on Facebook Share Update Your Profile to Receive Alerts Tailored to your Interests! on LinkedIn Share Update Your Profile to Receive Alerts Tailored to your Interests! on X Copy Link Customize your profile to receive tailored career content about the topics that matter most to you. Managing your preferences is … Read More Internship Guidelines for Staff/Faculty Share This: Share Internship Guidelines for Staff/Faculty on Facebook Share Internship Guidelines for Staff/Faculty on LinkedIn Share Internship Guidelines for Staff/Faculty on X Copy Link View Resource Federal Bureau of Investigation Public Service Announcement Share This: Share Federal Bureau of Investigation Public Service Announcement on Facebook Share Federal Bureau of Investigation Public Service Announcement on LinkedIn Share Federal Bureau of Investigation Public Service Announcement on X Copy Link View Resource View All Resources Facebook Instagram X (formerly Twitter) runsa@newark.rutgers.edu CARE Team © 2026 Rutgers University - Newark  |  All Rights Reserved Universitywide New Brunswick Camden RBHS MyRutgers Blackboard ScarletMail People Search Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution Privacy Policy | Terms of Service"
