iews from employees, and rankings of the best companies and industry employers. facebook instagram linkedin twitter Read More Vault Career Guide to Media and Entertainment, Second Edition Share This: Share Vault Career Guide to Media and Entertainment, Second Edition on Facebook Share Vault Career Guide to Media and Entertainment, Second Edition on LinkedIn Share Vault Career Guide to Media and Entertainment, Second Edition on X Copy Link The media and entertainment industry consists of movies, print, radio, television, electronic publications, and streaming video, and it offers a … Read More Vault Guide to Nanotechnology Jobs, Second Edition Share This: Share Vault Guide to Nanotechnology Jobs, Second Edition on Facebook Share Vault Guide to Nanotechnology Jobs, Second Edition on LinkedIn Share Vault Guide to Nanotechnology Jobs, Second Edition on X Copy Link The Vault Guides to Jobs series provides essential information about key careers and industries, with an emphasis on preparing for … Read More Vault Guide to Nursing Jobs Share This: Share Vault Guide to Nursing Jobs on Facebook Share Vault Guide to Nursing Jobs on LinkedIn Share Vault Guide to Nursing Jobs on X Copy Link The Vault Guides to Jobs series provides essential information about key careers and industries, with an emphasis on preparing for a career … Vault #9781438191461 Show author info A comprehensive resource for students and job seekers looking for career advice, job postings, company reviews from employees, and rankings of the best companies and industry employers. facebook instagram linkedin twitter Read More Vault Guide to Dance Jobs, Second Edition Share This: Share Vault Guide to Dance Jobs, Second Edition on Facebook Share Vault Guide to Dance Jobs, Second Edition on LinkedIn Share Vault Guide to Dance Jobs, Second Edition on X Copy Link The Vault Guides to Jobs series provides essential information about key careers and industries, with an emphasis on preparing for … Read More View All Resources Career Outcomes All Years Class of 2025 Class of 2024 Class of 2023 Class of 2022 Class of 2021 Class All Academic Divisions/Schools All Programs/Majors Toggle charts Rutgers University–Newark graduates enter the world prepared to make an impact. Through rigorous academics, career readiness programs, and hands-on experiences, our students develop the skills, confidence, and networks needed to thrive in their chosen fields. Each year, the Office of Career Resources & Exploration surveys graduating students to understand their post-graduation outcomes—employment, continuing education, and other pursuits. The results below reflect our commitment to transparency and the success of RU–N graduates within six months of completing their degrees. Our knowledge rate —the percentage of graduates for whom we can verify outcomes—has steadily increased over time, demonstrating growing engagement and data reliability: Class of 2025: 66% Class of 2024: 53.8% Class of 2023: 57.7% Class of 2022: 50.6% Class of 2021: 27.3% Explore the Results Use the filters below to view outcomes by graduation year , school , or major . Results update automatically as you make selections. All data align with the National Association of Colleges & Employers (NACE) standards for First Destination Surveys. 01 First Destination 02 Top Employers 03 Starting Salary 04 Employment Locations 05 Top Universities 06 Degree Types 07 Fields of Study Select data point First Destination Top Employers Starting Salary Employment Locations Top Universities Degree Types Fields of Study First Destination Post-Graduation Outcomes This section highlights what Rutgers University–Newark graduates are doing within six months of completing their degrees. It includes employment, continuing education, public service, and those still seeking opportunities. Top Employers Employers Hiring Rutgers–Newark Graduates Our graduates launch careers with organizations across every major sector—from global corporations to regional nonprofits and public agencies. These employers reflect the reach of Rutgers–Newark talent and the value of a RU–N degree in today’s workforce. Starting Salary The salary distribution below reflects reported starting salaries for full-time employed graduates. Salaries vary by industry, role, and experience, but Rutgers–Newark graduates consistently demonstrate strong earning potential early in their careers. Only categories with five or more responses are shown to protect student privacy. Employment Locations Where Our Graduates Launch Their Careers Rutgers–Newark graduates begin their professional journeys across New Jersey, the New York metropolitan area, and beyond. Many remain in the region to serve local communities, while others expand their impact nationally and internationally. United States World Top Universities Graduate and Professional Schools Many Rutgers–Newark alumni pursue advanced degrees at top universities nationwide. Graduates continue their studies in law, business, public policy, education, and health professions. Degree Types Degrees Represented in Outcomes Data This data includes outcomes from undergraduate and graduate students across Rutgers University–Newark’s academic divisions. Degree type helps contextualize employment and salary trends across programs. Fields of Study Academic Backgrounds of Graduates Rutgers–Newark graduates represent a wide range of disciplines—from business, arts, and sciences to health, public administration, and technology. This variety highlights the interdisciplinary strength and adaptability of RU–N students in the workforce. We don’t have enough student data to show you these results. Close Videos Career.io Career Pathways Video post Registered Nurse, Aurora Video post K-8 Spanish Teacher, Toledo Public Schools Video post Environmental Engineer and Entrepreneur, Advanced Oxidation Technology Video post Law Student, Valparaiso University Law School Video post Diversity in Finance – WayUp Office Hours Video post View All Videos Facebook Instagram X (formerly Twitter) runsa@newark.rutgers.edu CARE Team © 2026 Rutgers University - Newark  |  All Rights Reserved Universitywide New Brunswick Camden RBHS MyRutgers Blackboard ScarletMail People Search Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution Privacy Policy | Terms of Service"
    },
    "https://careers.newark.rutgers.edu/channels/exploring-multiple-interests/": {
      "title": "Exploring/Multiple Interests",
      "description": "Exploring/Multiple Interests – Career Resources and Exploration | Rutgers University – Newark Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Log in Sign up Guests Search Keywords Make an Appointment Rutgers-Newark Handshake Request a Workshop Home About Us Staff CRE Student Employees Student Outcomes People We Connect Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Campus Partners Faculty Employers/Recruiters Family Industry Pathways Exploring/Multiple Interests Arts, Media, & Entertainment Data & Technology Financial Services, Logistics, & Management Government, Law, & Public Policy Healthcare, Pharmaceuticals, & Sciences Natural Resources, Sustainability, & Environmental Science Nonprofit, Social Justice, & Education Explore Opportunities Detecting Fraudulent Job Postings Experiential Opportunities Jobs and Internships Job Searching Making Connections Rutgers Scarlet Service Internship (RSSI) Program Professional Resources CareerThreads – Free Professional Attire Raider Headshot Studio Majors and Careers Get Career Ready Career Ready in Real Life Resumes and Cover Letters Interviewing Graduate and Professional School Personal Statements Videos on Demand Events All Events Fall 2026 Raider Career and Internship Fair at Rutgers University-Newark Raider Career Impact Awards Exploring/Multiple Interests Latest News Virtual Work Experiences Featured Employers Career Resources Vault Guides About the Community If you are still deciding on a career industry or have interests in several industries, we encourage you to explore the information and resources on the specific industry pages. It is not just one single factor that determines one’s path. The key to making informed choices involves a combination of activities: self-exploration, research, and experiential engagement (e.g., student activities, volunteering). Moreover, making a decision about a career does not close off other possibilities. Most people’s careers will likely change direction 5-6 times over the course of their lifetime. As you explore your options, it may help for you to think about how those possibilities connect to who you are and what you want your career to represent. Here are a few factors to consider: Values (What’s important to you?) Personality (How do you describe yourself?) Interests (What do you enjoy?) Strengths (What is easy for you to do?) Skills (What can you do well?) Past experiences/activities (What has been meaningful to you?) Personal goals (short- and long-term) (What do you hope to do?) Sidebar Connect with Alumni Brad Golden Adjunct Professor, Rutgers Business School Learn more from Brad Nate Nakao Digital Marketing & Media Producer, Rutgers Law School Learn more from Nate Valline Whitsett-Hernandez Professional Paralegal & Notary Services, PPNS, LLC Learn more from Valline Erin Sweeney Equal Justice Works Fellow / Attorney, Kids in Need of Defense Learn more from Erin Benahir Crespo, MPA Bilingual Counselor, NEW JERSEY ASSOCIATION ON CORRECTION - NJAC Learn more from Benahir Anthony D’Arelli Learn more from Anthony Veenit Singh Career Coach - Refugee Services, JVS Boston Learn more from Veenit Andrew Stein Founder, The After Parties Learn more from Andrew Jane Sharp Director, NJ Certified Public Manager Program, Rutgers School of Public Affairs and Administration Learn more from Jane Mikal Naeem Nash Historian, Essex County College Learn more from Mikal Naeem Chuck La Tournous Vice President, Marketing, Multiple Line Agencies, American National Learn more from Chuck Amanda Schwartz Associate attorney, Reed Smith LLP Learn more from Amanda View All People Latest News 6 of 10 Top Paying Majors in Engineering College Minor vs. Double Major: Which Is Better for Your Career in 2026? What Are the Best Majors for Your Personality? Discovering Your Career Purpose And Passion 5 New Companies to Discover on The Muse View All Virtual Work Experiences Showcase your skills. Find your career fit. Forage offers bite-sized 5-6 hour virtua