. In these industries are careers that use a variety of methods to produce creative content, tell stories, or share information.  The methods used can include writing, theater, music, literature, film, sculpture and paintings and drawings. Sample Job Roles/Functions Here are some job roles/functions that are a part of the Arts, Media, and Entertainment industries. As you continue to explore, you’ll find many more. Actor Author Media Buyer Digital/Interactive Media Creator Video/Film Production Assistant Graphic Artist Journalist Medical Illustrator Musician Content Marketing Coordinator Public Relations Specialist Recording/Digitization Technician Web Content Developer/Writer Production Assistant Related Majors at Rutgers-Newark Below you will find a list of majors at Rutgers-Newark that will provide you with academic knowledge related to this industry: African American & African Studies Anthropology Art English Graphic Design History Journalism & Media Studies Marketing Music Philosophy Portuguese & Lusophone Studies Sociology Spanish Theater Video Production Visual Arts Women & Gender Studies While recruiting timelines may vary from employer to employer, it’s helpful to know when the top recruiting times are for your industry. Take a look at the timeline below to help you learn when to prepare for your job search, and click on the timeline to learn more! Sidebar Featured Jobs & Internships Social Media Video Editor Intern Samantha Siu New York Advertising/Marketing Intern Phantom Fireworks Companies Accounting Intern Phantom Fireworks Companies Social & Content Intern Olivela Rotational Sports Internship 2aDays See All Jobs Connect with Alumni Brad Golden Adjunct Professor, Rutgers Business School Learn more from Brad Nate Nakao Digital Marketing & Media Producer, Rutgers Law School Learn more from Nate Haiyan Liu Career Counselor, Rutgers Learn more from Haiyan Valline Whitsett-Hernandez Professional Paralegal & Notary Services, PPNS, LLC Learn more from Valline 