ces, Logistics and Management industries.   In these industries are careers that involve the investment and management of money and assets, the flow of goods from one place to another which integrates the planning and distribution of resources, and the coordination of activities of an organization in order to achieve defined objectives. Sample Job Roles/Functions Here are some job roles/functions that are a part of Financial Services, Logistics and Management industries.  As you continue to explore, you’ll find many more. Accountant Claims Adjuster Cost Estimator Economist Financial Analyst Management Trainee Underwriter Investment Banker Logistics Analyst Market Research Analyst Operations Manager Supply Chain Manager Related majors at Rutgers-Newark Below you will find a list of majors at Rutgers-Newark that will provide you with academic knowledge related to this industry: Accounting Applied Math Economics Finance Math Management Supply Chain Management While recruiting timelines may vary from employer to employer, it’s helpful to know when the top recruiting times are for your industry. Take a look at the timeline below to help you learn when to prepare for your job search, and click on the timeline to learn more! Sidebar Featured Jobs & Internships Trade Marketing Intern Colombina Candy Company, Inc. Controls Systems Engineer SharkNinja Part-Time Warehouse Associate HJ Kirby Corporation Weekend Warehouse Associate Vilure Group LLC Customer Service  and Sales Intern BoxUp See All Jobs Connect with Alumni Brad Golden Adjunct Professor, Rutgers Business School Learn more from Brad Haiyan Liu Career Counselor, Rutgers Learn more from Haiyan Valline Whitsett-Hernandez Professional Paralegal & Notary Services, PPNS, LLC Learn more from Valline Michael C. Chiusano Wealth Management Analyst, Morgan Stanley Learn more from Michael C. Italo Moreno Area Operations Manager, Amazon Learn more from Italo Babatunde P. Odubekun Vice President & Counsel, CleanCapital Learn more