e, and Education. In these industries are careers in organizations that serve the public good, that are concerned with principles of human rights, equity how individuals are able to access all aspects of society, and the learning process for individuals to attain knowledge. Sample Job Roles/Functions Here are some job roles/functions that are a part of Nonprofit, Social Justice and Education industries. As you continue to explore, you’ll find many more. Case Manager Community Organizer Development Officer Grant Writer Nonprofit Manager Educator School Counselor Social Worker Student Affairs Coordinator Victim Advocate Related majors at Rutgers-Newark Below you will find a list of majors at Rutgers-Newark that will provide you with academic knowledge related to this industry: Applied Math African American & African Studies Anthropology Biology Chemistry Criminal Justice Economics Education (teacher certification) English Environmental Sciences Geological Sciences History Math Philosophy Physics Political Science Portuguese & Lusophone Studies Psychology Public & Nonprofit Administration Social Work Sociology Spanish Women & Gender Studies While recruiting timelines may vary from employer to employer, it’s helpful to know when the top recruiting times are for your industry. Take a look at the timeline below to help you learn when to prepare for your job search, and click on the timeline to learn more! Sidebar Featured Jobs & Internships Strategic Communications & Social Media (Fall 2026/Spring 2027/Summer 2027)) The Institute of World Politics Human Resources Intern Matheny Medical and Educational Center Marketing Intern Lapeer Christian Counseling, LLC Campus Recreation Intern - Special Projects Florida Atlantic University Events And Communications (Fall 2026/Spring 2027/Summer2027) The Institute of World Politics See All Jobs Connect with Alumni Valline Whitsett-Hernandez Professional Paralegal & Notary Services, PPNS, LLC Learn more from Valline Gissell Xochimitl C