r on X Copy Link “Feel empowered and respected by speaking up and being who you are. The Intercultural Resource Center (IRC) is the space … Read More View All Resources Vault Guides Skip filter options to posts Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Resource Categories: Advising Guidelines Applications Career Guides Hiring Policies How-tos & Examples Industry Reports Professional Writing Samples Third Party Resources Vault Guides Close Clear Filters Vault Career Guide to Education, Third Edition Share This: Share Vault Career Guide to Education, Third Edition on Facebook Share Vault Career Guide to Education, Third Edition on LinkedIn Share Vault Career Guide to Education, Third Edition on X Copy Link Nearly one in four Americans is an enrolled student at any given time. As a result of this great demand … Read More Vault Guide to Social Sciences Jobs, Second Edition Share This: Share Vault Guide to Social Sciences Jobs, Second Edition on Facebook Share Vault Guide to Social Sciences Jobs, Second Edition on LinkedIn Share Vault Guide to Social Sciences Jobs, Second Edition on X Copy Link The Vault Guides to Jobs series provides essential information about key careers and industries, with an emphasis on preparing for … Read More Vault Guide to Writing and Editing Jobs, Second Edition Share This: Share Vault Guide to Writing and Editing Jobs, Second Edition on Facebook Share Vault Guide to Writing and Editing Jobs, Second Edition on LinkedIn Share Vault Guide to Writing and Editing Jobs, Second Edition on X Copy Link The Vault Guides to Jobs series provides essential information about key careers and industries, with an emphasis on preparing for … Read More Vault Guide to Social Services Jobs, Second Edition Share This: Share Vault Guide to Social Services Jobs, Second Edition on Facebook Share Vault Guide to Social Services Jobs, Second Edition on LinkedIn Share Vault Guide to Social Services Jobs, Second Edition on X Copy Link The Vault Guides to Jobs series provides essential information about key careers and industries, with an emphasis on preparing for … Read More Vault Career Guide to Consulting, Third Edition Share This: Share Vault Career Guide to Consulting, Third Edition on Facebook Share Vault Career Guide to Consulting, Third Edition on LinkedIn Share Vault Career Guide to Consulting, Third Edition on X Copy Link Consulting is a massive, international industry with global revenues of around $506 billion. It spans human resources, business advisory services, … Read More Vault Career Guide to Law, Third Edition Share This: Share Vault Career Guide to Law, Third Edition on Facebook Share Vault Career Guide to Law, Third Edition on LinkedIn Share Vault Career Guide to Law, Third Edition on X Copy Link Lawyers provide legal advice and representation to companies and individuals regarding hundreds of issues, such as civil rights, criminal offenses, … Read More View All Resources Career Outcomes All Years Class of 2025 Class of 2024 Class of 2023 Class of 2022 Class of 2021 Class All Academic Divisions/Schools All Programs/Majors Toggle charts Rutgers University–Newark graduates enter the world prepared to make an impact. Through rigorous academics, career readiness programs, and hands-on experiences, our students develop the skills, confidence, and networks needed to thrive in their chosen fields. Each year, the Office of Career Resources & Exploration surveys graduating students to understand their post-graduation outcomes—employment, continuing education, and other pursuits. The results below reflect our commitment to transparency and the success of RU–N graduates within six months of completing their degrees. Our knowledge rate —the percentage of graduates for whom we can verify outcomes—has steadily increased over time, demonstrating growing engagement and data reliability: Class of 2025: 66% Class of 2024: 53.8% Class of 2023: 57.7% Class of 2022: 50.6% Class of 2021: 27.3% Explore the Results Use the filters below to view outcomes by graduation year , school , or major . Results update automatically as you make selections. All data align with the National Association of Colleges & Employers (NACE) standards for First Destination Surveys. 01 First Destination 02 Top Employers 03 Starting Salary 04 Employment Locations 05 Top Universities 06 Degree Types 07 Fields of Study Select data point First Destination Top Employers Starting Salary Employment Locations Top Universities Degree Types Fields of Study First Destination Post-Graduation Outcomes This section highlights what Rutgers University–Newark graduates are doing within six months of completing their degrees. It includes employment, continuing education, public service, and those still seeking opportunities. Top Employers Employers Hiring Rutgers–Newark Graduates Our graduates launch careers with organizations across every major sector—from global corporations to regional nonprofits and public agencies. These employers reflect the reach of Rutgers–Newark talent and the value of a RU–N degree in today’s workforce. Starting Salary The salary distribution below reflects reported starting salaries for full-time employed graduates. Salaries vary by industry, role, and experience, but Rutgers–Newark graduates consistently demonstrate strong earning potential early in their careers. Only categories with five or more responses are shown to protect student privacy. Employment Locations Where Our Graduates Launch Their Careers Rutgers–Newark graduates begin their professional journeys across New Jersey, the New York metropolitan area, and beyond. Many remain in the region to serve local communities, while others expand their impact nationally and internationally. United States World Top Universities Graduate and Professional Schools Many Rutgers–Newark alumni pursue advanced degrees at top universities nationwide. Graduates continue their studies in law, business, public policy, education, and health professions. Degree Types Degrees Represented in Outcomes Data This data includes outcomes from undergraduate and graduate students across Rutgers University–Newark’s academic divisions. Degree type helps contextualize employment and salary trends across programs. Fields of Study Academic Backgrounds of Graduates Rutgers–Newark graduates represent a wide range of disciplines—from business, arts, and sciences to health, public administration, and technology. This variety highlights the interdisciplinary strength and adaptability of RU–N students in the workforce. We don’t have enough student data to show you these results. Close Videos K-8 Spanish Teacher, Toledo Public Schools Video post View All Videos Facebook Instagram X (formerly Twitter) runsa@newark.rutgers.edu CARE Team © 2026 Rutgers University - Newark  |  All Rights Reserved Universitywide New Brunswick Camden RBHS MyRutgers Blackboard ScarletMail People Search Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution Privacy Policy | Terms of Service"
