    "https://careers.newark.rutgers.edu/channels/experiential-opportunities/": {
      "title": "Experiential Opportunities",
      "description": "Experiential Opportunities – Career Resources and Exploration | Rutgers University – Newark Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Log in Sign up Guests Search Keywords Make an Appointment Rutgers-Newark Handshake Request a Workshop Home About Us Staff CRE Student Employees Student Outcomes People We Connect Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Campus Partners Faculty Employers/Recruiters Family Industry Pathways Exploring/Multiple Interests Arts, Media, & Entertainment Data & Technology Financial Services, Logistics, & Management Government, Law, & Public Policy Healthcare, Pharmaceuticals, & Sciences Natural Resources, Sustainability, & Environmental Science Nonprofit, Social Justice, & Education Explore Opportunities Detecting Fraudulent Job Postings Experiential Opportunities Jobs and Internships Job Searching Making Connections Rutgers Scarlet Service Internship (RSSI) Program Professional Resources CareerThreads – Free Professional Attire Raider Headshot Studio Majors and Careers Get Career Ready Career Ready in Real Life Resumes and Cover Letters Interviewing Graduate and Professional School Personal Statements Videos on Demand Events All Events Fall 2026 Raider Career and Internship Fair at Rutgers University-Newark Raider Career Impact Awards Experiential Opportunities Experiential opportunities are hands-on learning experiences in real-life settings. For any career goal, whether you’re actively searching for a job or still narrowing down your interests, getting real-world experience is essential. You’ll learn how your skills work in action as you refine your knowledge about possible career paths. Sharing the experiences you’ve completed on your application materials and in your interviews is an effective way to share your story as a candidate for internships, jobs, graduate school, professional school, or other goals. Use the links below for more details on experiential opportunities available for Rutgers students! If you’re looking to view and apply for jobs and internships, click here! Volunteering Industry/Field Experiences Academic Experiences Forage Virtual Work Experiences Fellowships Success Stories & Testimonials On-Campus Student Employment Part-time Jobs Internships & Cooperative Education Full-time Jobs Volunteering Volunteer experience allows you to learn about an organization, much like a job shadow or field experience, while also making a difference in your community. There are some opportunities for civic engagement that are paid, but for the most part, these are unpaid opportunities that help you develop community-based knowledge, values, and skills. Students often wonder if they should list volunteer experiences on their resume, and the answer is almost always yes! Volunteer experience on your resume shows employers that you take initiative and care about your community—valuable attributes in any candidate! El Rio Health View All Jobs Highlander Charter School View All Jobs Compostela Cathedral Prep View All Jobs New Jersey Coalition to End Homelessness View All Jobs THE AM TO PM WELLBEING SERVICE LIMITED View All Jobs Paper Airplanes View All Jobs View More Industry/Field Experiences Many academic programs require some type of industry or field experience as part of a course or other graduation prerequisite. These hands-on experiences and the connections you make in fieldwork and job shadowing are fantastic ways to see a day in the life of a career or organization. If you are looking for short-term or virtual option, consider exploring a micro-internship! Even if the experience was short-term or required as part of a course, it’s important to still list it on your resume and talk about it in interviews. If you’d like more information on internships or paid opportunities, click here! Micro-Internships with Parker Dewey Urban Education Field Experiences Rutgers School of Social Work: Office of Field Education Rutgers Law School: Field Placement Opportunities in Newark View More Academic Experiences There are so many opportunities to build your career skills through opportunities available at Rutgers. Here are a few examples of academic experiences that you can add to your resume to showcase your career readiness. Courses may count as experiential if they involve hands-on learning. Check with your academic advisor to see what options are available within your major! Study abroad is an opportunity to live and take classes in a foreign country, immerse in the culture, learn a language, and gain global perspective. What a great way to show an employer your ability to adapt to new settings and develop your cultural competency! Leadership programs provide skill-building activities that promote teamwork and networking opportunities. On-campus programs allow you to meet other students and university staff as you put career-readiness skills into action, while off-campus programs build your network with professional organizations and can provide a “sneak peek” into an organization. Research is often conducted through an academic department and can be paid or unpaid. Many students say that these experiences allowed them to get valuable advice from faculty while giving them practical experience in collaborating with a team to work towards a common goal. Road to Wall Street Program Rutgers Online Global Learning Millenium Fellowship: Leadership Development Program Braven Accelerator: Spring 2022 Rutgers Study Abroad Information Study Abroad Program Catalog View More Forage Experiences Showcase your skills. Find your career fit. Forage offers bite-sized 5-6 hour virtual work experience programs that give you a genuine career advantage with Fortune 500 companies. These opportunities are completely free, with no prior experience or application needed to get started. They're a great way to try out different fields and see what you like before applying for internships or jobs! Banking at PNC: Building Career Skills Experience with PNC PNC Client Service Experience with Bloomberg Bloomberg Data Visualisation: Empowering Business with Effective Insights Experience with Tata Tata Introduction to Commercial Law Experience with Mallesons Mallesons Introduction to Campus Recruitment Experience with Forage Academy Forage Academy Unspoken Interview Fundamentals Experience with Comcast Comcast View All Experiences Fellowships A fellowship is a way for students, typically graduate or doctoral students, to get funding to support their education and training. They are available for a range of academic areas and organizations, and often involve an application process in order for students to be selected based on certain criteria. See below for fellowships that you can apply for today! JPG Enterprises View All Jobs Capital Fellows Programs View All Jobs Neuhaus Education Center View All Jobs Grace Bible Church View All Jobs Foster Success View All Jobs Rich Earth Institute View All Jobs View More Success Stories & Testimonials Students like you are participating in all kinds of experiences, making the most of their time in college and preparing for whatever comes next! Read their stories to get the inside scoop on what they did and learned, then get inspired to find your next opportunity! Student Perspective: Landing a Paid Summer Internship No Internship? Here Are 9 Ways to Get Work Experience This Summer Wondering how your courses and college experiences connect to your career? Turning Volunteer Experience into Work Experience Study Abroad: Stories About Career Impact View More Career Resources Micro-Internships with Parker Dewey Share This: Share Micro-Internships with Parker Dewey on Facebook Share Micro-Internships with Parker Dewey on LinkedIn Share Micro-Internships with Parker Dewey on X Copy Link “Students from all majors can execute professional assignments to build and demonstrate skills while exploring a variety of career paths.” View Resource Rutgers-Newark Handshake Share This: Share Rutgers-Newark Handshake on Facebook Share Rutgers-Newark Handshake on LinkedIn Share Rutgers-Newark Handshake on X Copy Link Handshake helps students find the experiences they need to get career ready. From events like career fairs and workshops, to … Read More Rutgers Scarlet Service Internship (RSSI) Program Share This: Share Rutgers Scarlet Service Internship (RSSI) Program on Facebook Share Rutgers Scarlet Service Internship (RSSI) Program on LinkedIn Share Rutgers Scarlet Service Internship (RSSI) Program on X Copy Link Fostering Civic Engagement & Career Readiness Rutgers Scarlet Service establishes civic engagement as central to a Rutgers education—fostering appreciation of … Read More Forage Share This: Share Forage on Facebook Share Forage on LinkedIn Share Forage on X Copy Link Showcase your skills. Find your career fit.\nAt Forage, our virtual work experience programs give students the opportunity to learn … Read More View All Resources Videos How To Land Internships as a Freshman and Sophomore in College Video post View All Videos Facebook Instagram X (formerly Twitter) runsa@newark.rutgers.edu CARE Team © 2026 Rutgers University - Newark  |  All Rights Reserved Universitywide New Brunswick Camden RBHS MyRutgers Blackboard ScarletMail People Search Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution Privacy Policy | Terms of Service"
