    "https://careers.newark.rutgers.edu/channels/jobs-and-internships/": {
      "title": "Jobs and Internships",
      "description": "Jobs and Internships – Career Resources and Exploration | Rutgers University – Newark Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Log in Sign up Guests Search Keywords Make an Appointment Rutgers-Newark Handshake Request a Workshop Home About Us Staff CRE Student Employees Student Outcomes People We Connect Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Campus Partners Faculty Employers/Recruiters Family Industry Pathways Exploring/Multiple Interests Arts, Media, & Entertainment Data & Technology Financial Services, Logistics, & Management Government, Law, & Public Policy Healthcare, Pharmaceuticals, & Sciences Natural Resources, Sustainability, & Environmental Science Nonprofit, Social Justice, & Education Explore Opportunities Detecting Fraudulent Job Postings Experiential Opportunities Jobs and Internships Job Searching Making Connections Rutgers Scarlet Service Internship (RSSI) Program Professional Resources CareerThreads – Free Professional Attire Raider Headshot Studio Majors and Careers Get Career Ready Career Ready in Real Life Resumes and Cover Letters Interviewing Graduate and Professional School Personal Statements Videos on Demand Events All Events Fall 2026 Raider Career and Internship Fair at Rutgers University-Newark Raider Career Impact Awards Jobs and Internships Searching for internships and jobs can take lots of time and effort. That’s why we pulled together a variety of opportunities on this page to help you start your search! Use this page to learn more about employers and the types of positions they are hiring for and find opportunities that match your interests and skills. Remember, the Office of Career Resources and Exploration is here to help you. As you’re preparing to apply for jobs, you’ll want to update your application materials and prepare for interviews (don’t wait until an interview is offered—practice beforehand so you’re ready when the offer comes!). Jobs and internships aren’t the only way to build your resume and professional portfolio. Click here for experiential opportunities that you can participate in today that will give you the skills and experiences employers are looking for! Volunteering Industry/Field Experiences Academic Experiences Forage Virtual Work Experiences Fellowships Success Stories & Testimonials On-Campus Student Employment Part-time Jobs Internships & Cooperative Education Full-time Jobs Sidebar Latest News How to Negotiate Your First Job Offer in 2026 How to leverage your summer internship into a full-time offer Yes, it’s July and, no, it’s not too late to land an internship Win the summer: Top 10 job search sites for seasonal work and internships How to Get Work Experience This Summer Without an Internship View All On Campus Student Employment On-campus employment is a great way to financially support your academic pursuits while also adding an experience that you can put on your resume. Just like any job, internship, or other experiential opportunity, your on-campus job provides the opportunity to build career-readiness skills like teamwork, communication, and critical thinking. See the opportunities for on-campus employment below to get started! If you’re interested in other ways to gain experience, click here! University of the Pacific Clinical Nutrition View All Jobs Career Resources and Exploration Select View All Jobs Rutgers - New Brunswick View All Jobs View More Part-time Jobs If you want to gain career experience while earning money, but don’t have the space in your schedule for full-time employment, a part-time job could be a great option! You’ll learn about an organization and build your professional network, while still having time to take class, get involved on campus, spend time with your family, and support any other priorities in your life. See who’s hiring by viewing the employers and their available opportunities below! Shoe Shack Martin/Union City View All Jobs the DAISY View All Jobs Essence Extractors View All Jobs Tentac Enterprises View All Jobs Croasdaile Country Club View All Jobs Gymnastic Sports Academy View All Jobs View More Internships & Cooperative Education Internships and cooperative Education (more commonly called a co-op) are great ways for college students to get practical experience in the field while building their professional experience. They also give employers the opportunity to guide and evaluate talent. To learn more about internships, click here to see NACE’s perspectives and criteria for internships. To learn more about co-ops, click here to read NACE’s research on various approaches to co-ops and what makes them distinct from internships. Olivela View All Jobs T-Swirl Crepe View All Jobs CEBRA View All Jobs MBM Golf Lab View All Jobs Colombina Candy Company, Inc. View All Jobs SharkNinja View All Jobs View More Full-time Jobs Employers want to hire Rutgers-Newark students! Even if you’re not in an active search, you can explore the opportunities below to learn more about what types of positions employers are looking for, what skills they value, and what you need to do to start your application. If you’re ready to take the next step in your career journey, apply for your next opportunity today! Skida Headwear & Accessories View All Jobs POSTNET View All Jobs Miller Sellner View All Jobs Van-Griner Learning View All Jobs View More Career Resources Micro-Internships with Parker Dewey Share This: Share Micro-Internships with Parker Dewey on Facebook Share Micro-Internships with Parker Dewey on LinkedIn Share Micro-Internships with Parker Dewey on X Copy Link “Students from all majors can execute professional assignments to build and demonstrate skills while exploring a variety of career paths.” View Resource Rutgers-Newark Handshake Share This: Share Rutgers-Newark Handshake on Facebook Share Rutgers-Newark Handshake on LinkedIn Share Rutgers-Newark Handshake on X Copy Link Handshake helps students find the experiences they need to get career ready. From events like career fairs and workshops, to … Read More Rutgers Scarlet Service Internship (RSSI) Program Share This: Share Rutgers Scarlet Service Internship (RSSI) Program on Facebook Share Rutgers Scarlet Service Internship (RSSI) Program on LinkedIn Share Rutgers Scarlet Service Internship (RSSI) Program on X Copy Link Fostering Civic Engagement & Career Readiness Rutgers Scarlet Service establishes civic engagement as central to a Rutgers education—fostering appreciation of … Read More Five-Step Process to the Job Search Share This: Share Five-Step Process to the Job Search on Facebook Share Five-Step Process to the Job Search on LinkedIn Share Five-Step Process to the Job Search on X Copy Link The job search can be an exciting time, but it can also be a time of uncertainty. If you’re feeling … Read More View All Resources Videos Career.io Seven Stories Exercise Video post Rutgers-Newark Handshake Tutorial Video post View All Videos Facebook Instagram X (formerly Twitter) runsa@newark.rutgers.edu CARE Team © 2026 Rutgers University - Newark  |  All Rights Reserved Universitywide New Brunswick Camden RBHS MyRutgers Blackboard ScarletMail People Search Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution Privacy Policy | Terms of Service"
    },
    "https://careers.newark.rutgers.edu/channels/job-searching/": {
      "title": "Job Searching",
      "description": "Job Searching – Career Resources and Exploration | Rutgers University – Newark Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Log in Sign up Guests Search Keywords Make an Appointment Rutgers-Newark Handshake Request a Workshop Home About Us Staff CRE Student Employees Student Outcomes People We Connect Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Campus Partners Faculty Employers/Recruiters Family Industry Pathways Exploring/Multiple Interests Arts, Media, & Entertainment Data & Technology Financial Services, Logistics, & Management Government, Law, & Public Policy Healthcare, Pharmaceuticals, & Sciences Natural Resources, Sustainability, & Environmental Science Nonprofit, Social Justice, & Education Explore Opportunities Detecting Fraudulent Job Postings Experiential Opportunities Jobs and Internships Job Searching Making Connections Rutgers Scarlet Service Internship (RSSI) Program Professional Resources CareerThreads – Free Professional Attire Raider Headshot Studio Majors and Careers Get Career Ready Career Ready in Real Life Resumes and Cover Letters Interviewing Graduate and Professional School Personal Statements Videos on Demand Events All Events Fall 2026 Raider Career and Internship Fair at Rutgers University-Newark Raider Career Impact Awards Job Searching Latest News Latest News Forage Experiences Career Resources Vault Guides Videos We get it. Job searching can be stressful! Knowing where to look to find opportunities, getting all of your documents organized, preparing for both rejections and acceptances, there’s so much to think about. Wherever you are in the job search process, this page has tips for you. Some of it might sound pretty familiar, like getting your resume and cover letter ready. But there might be some things you haven’t thought about, like managing your mindset and gauging the company culture in your interview. Here are five steps to creating a focused and flexible job search plan: 1. Look Understand what’s happening in the industry you would like to pursue. Review the information on our industry pages , or use the tools within Steppingblocks . To get a customized newsletter with advice, events, and helpful information, click here for instructions on how to set up your profile. 2. Reflect Review the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) career readiness competencies . Think about your experiences, and write down situations in which you’ve demonstrated those skills. Ensure your resume exemplifies your skills and is ready to pass initial screening stages. Uploading your resume to Quinncia only takes a few minutes, and you’ll get fast feedback on what to improve. 3. Strategize Your job search plan will likely need to be expanded beyond searching for positions that are directly tied to your ideal career goal. Consider pursuing other experiential opportunities or jobs and internships that can help you boost your skills. LinkedIn Learning is available for free to you, using your netID and password, and has a wide range of courses that will help you get career ready. 4. Connect Staying connected with peers, finding potential mentors, and meeting others within your industry will help you in your career path. Rutgers-Newark Handshake can be a place to search for peers who have similar interests. If you’d like to find alumni, you can use Rutgers Student Alumni Career Connect or the connect with Rutgers-Newark alums on LinkedIn . 5. Act Rutgers-Newark Handshake is a good place to start looking for job postings, as employers post there to seek entry-level talent, as well as candidates with a few years of experience. Review our tips on resumes and cover letters . Make sure that the skills you mention in your application documents align with the skills in job postings, always tailor your resume for each position, and always get your resume reviewed before submitting. Want to learn more? Scroll down for resources and articles to help you navigate the job search! Latest News The new grad job search playbook: Where to look, what to fix, and how to network How to Negotiate Your First Job Offer in 2026 The Ultimate Job Search Checklist for College Seniors in 2026 What Do People Use Instead of LinkedIn? 7 Alternatives for Job Seekers in 2026 Ghosted by an employer? How to take your power back in your job search | From Dorms to Desks Podcast | ep100 View All Career Resources Rutgers-Newark Handshake Share This: Share Rutgers-Newark Handshake on Facebook Share Rutgers-Newark Handshake on LinkedIn Share Rutgers-Newark Handshake on X Copy Link Handshake helps students find the experiences they need to get career ready. From events like career fairs and workshops, to … Read More 50 Free Zoom Video Backgrounds To Look Professional On Calls Share This: Share 50 Free Zoom Video Backgrounds To Look Professional On Calls on Facebook Share 50 Free Zoom Video Backgrounds To Look Professional On Calls on LinkedIn Share 50 Free Zoom Video Backgrounds To Look Professional On Calls on X Copy Link View Resource 40 Templates to Help You Handle Your Toughest Work Emails Share This: Share 40 Templates to Help You Handle Your Toughest Work Emails on Facebook Share 40 Templates to Help You Handle Your Toughest Work Emails on LinkedIn Share 40 Templates to Help You Handle Your Toughest Work Emails on X Copy Link Email templates for just about any job searching or in-the-workplace scenario you might encounter! Get the Templates Five-Step Process to the Job Search Share This: Share Five-Step Process to the Job Search on Facebook Share Five-Step Process to the Job Search on LinkedIn Share Five-Step Process to the Job Search on X Copy Link The job search can be an exciting time, but it can also be a time of uncertainty. If you’re feeling … Read More Job Search Tracking Spreadsheet Share This: Share Job Search Tracking Spreadsheet on Facebook Share Job Search Tracking Spreadsheet on LinkedIn Share Job Search Tracking Spreadsheet on X Copy Link Use this spreadsheet template to stay organized throughout your job search! View Resource 2021 Top 50 Companies for Diversity List Share This: Share 2021 Top 50 Companies for Diversity List on Facebook Share 2021 Top 50 Companies for Diversity List on LinkedIn Share 2021 Top 50 Companies for Diversity List on X Copy Link The DiversityInc Top 50 Companies for Diversity process began in 2001 and is the leading assessment of diversity management in … Read More View All Resources Vault Guides Skip filter options to posts Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Resource Categories: Advising Guidelines Applications Career Guides Hiring Policies How-tos & Examples Industry Reports Professional Writing Samples Third Party Resources Vault Guides Close Clear Filters The Vault Guide to Resumes and Job-Hunting Skills, Second Edition Share This: Share The Vault Guide to Resumes and Job-Hunting Skills, Second Edition on Facebook Share The Vault Guide to Resumes and Job-Hunting Skills, Second Edition on LinkedIn Share The Vault Guide to Resumes and Job-Hunting Skills, Second Edition on X Copy Link It takes more than a solid résumé and cover letter to make yourself stand out to prospective employers. Networking and … Vault #9781438148465 Show author info A comprehensive resource for students and job seekers looking for career advice, job postings, company reviews from employees, and rankings of the best companies and industry employers. facebook instagram linkedin twitter Read More View All Resources Videos Career.io Seven Stories Exercise Video post Rutgers-Newark Handshake Tutorial Video post View All Videos Facebook Instagram X (formerly Twitter) runsa@newark.rutgers.edu CARE Team © 2026 Rutgers University - Newark  |  All Rights Reserved Universitywide New Brunswick Camden RBHS MyRutgers Blackboard ScarletMail People Search Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution Privacy Policy | Terms of Service"
