    "https://careers.newark.rutgers.edu/channels/making-connections/": {
      "title": "Making Connections",
      "description": "Making Connections – Career Resources and Exploration | Rutgers University – Newark Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Log in Sign up Guests Search Keywords Make an Appointment Rutgers-Newark Handshake Request a Workshop Home About Us Staff CRE Student Employees Student Outcomes People We Connect Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Campus Partners Faculty Employers/Recruiters Family Industry Pathways Exploring/Multiple Interests Arts, Media, & Entertainment Data & Technology Financial Services, Logistics, & Management Government, Law, & Public Policy Healthcare, Pharmaceuticals, & Sciences Natural Resources, Sustainability, & Environmental Science Nonprofit, Social Justice, & Education Explore Opportunities Detecting Fraudulent Job Postings Experiential Opportunities Jobs and Internships Job Searching Making Connections Rutgers Scarlet Service Internship (RSSI) Program Professional Resources CareerThreads – Free Professional Attire Raider Headshot Studio Majors and Careers Get Career Ready Career Ready in Real Life Resumes and Cover Letters Interviewing Graduate and Professional School Personal Statements Videos on Demand Events All Events Fall 2026 Raider Career and Internship Fair at Rutgers University-Newark Raider Career Impact Awards Making Connections Latest News Latest News Forage Experiences Career Resources Vault Guides Videos Connecting with others is an important part of your career preparation. Through these connections, you can learn more about different careers, understand what’s expected in different industries, or hear about upcoming opportunities.\r\n\r\nHow do you find people? Make a list of everyone you know and identify how they could help you gather career information or experience. Who do you know at school? Professors, friends, and even friends’ parents can all be helpful contacts. Did you hold a part-time job? Volunteer? Have an internship? Think about the people you came into contact with there.\r\n\r\nRemember to be courteous and tactful in all your conversations. Whether your conversation is in person, on the phone, or via e-mail, follow up with a thank-you note to show your appreciation and improve your chances of creating a productive relationship.Finally, making connections is not just about the benefit to you! Find ways to share information with the people you meet, and help others as well.\r\n\r\nHow do you share your story? Prepare Reflect on the information you want others to know about you. This information could include:\r\n\r\nCourses you’re taking/have taken\r\nExperiences that you’re pursuing/have pursued (internships, volunteering, student organizations, jobs)\r\n\r\nGoals you have in mind for your future\r\nConsider who your audience is, and what information may be most relevant to that audience. Listen Remember to listen to the person in front of you.\r\nShow that you’re paying attention with non-verbal communication, including eye contact, nodding, smiling.\r\n\r\nFocus on what is being shared with you, and not just on the next thing you want to say. Respond Consider how to incorporate your story with the story of the person you’re meeting. This may be finding commonalities, asking questions that build upon the conversation.\r\nRemember to be courteous and tactful in all your conversations. Whether your conversation is in person, on the phone, or via e-mail, follow up with a thank-you note to show your appreciation and improve your chances of creating a productive relationship.\r\n\r\nFinally, making connections is not just about the benefit to you! Find ways to share information with the people you meet, and help others as well. Resources Rutgers Student Alumni Career Connect (In Rutgers-Newark Handshake, go to Career Center—Resources to log in) LinkedIn (Tip: search for Rutgers University –Newark. From the school page, you can select the Alumni section to search for alumni Latest News 8 Awesome Women’s Professional Networks What Is Networking and Why Is it Important? What Do People Use Instead of LinkedIn? 7 Alternatives for Job Seekers in 2026 Strategies for Maintaining Professional Relationships During Career Transitions Building a professional network in a digital world: A guide for college students and new grads View All Career Resources Tips for Talking to Graduate/Professional School Recruiters Share This: Share Tips for Talking to Graduate/Professional School Recruiters on Facebook Share Tips for Talking to Graduate/Professional School Recruiters on LinkedIn Share Tips for Talking to Graduate/Professional School Recruiters on X Copy Link Potential questions to ask: What are your graduates prepared to do?\nWhat areas do your grads work in?\nAre there … Read More Rutgers-Newark Handshake Share This: Share Rutgers-Newark Handshake on Facebook Share Rutgers-Newark Handshake on LinkedIn Share Rutgers-Newark Handshake on X Copy Link Handshake helps students find the experiences they need to get career ready. From events like career fairs and workshops, to … Read More How to Ask a Professor for Research Opportunities: Share This: Share How to Ask a Professor for Research Opportunities: on Facebook Share How to Ask a Professor for Research Opportunities: on LinkedIn Share How to Ask a Professor for Research Opportunities: on X Copy Link Research the Professors and their background\nLook on Linked In\nSearch for faculty profiles on RUN’s website\nEmail them!\nHave … Read More Entry Point! Share This: Share Entry Point! on Facebook Share Entry Point! on LinkedIn Share Entry Point! on X Copy Link Entry Point!, a signature program of the AAAS Project on Science, Technology and Disability, is a national effort to discover … Read More Lime Connect Share This: Share Lime Connect on Facebook Share Lime Connect on LinkedIn Share Lime Connect on X Copy Link Lime Connect represents the largest network of high potential university students and professionals who happen to have disabilities in the world. … Read More Rutgers Student-Alumni Career Connect Share This: Share Rutgers Student-Alumni Career Connect on Facebook Share Rutgers Student-Alumni Career Connect on LinkedIn Share Rutgers Student-Alumni Career Connect on X Copy Link Want to connect with alumni mentors and professionals to build your network? Check out Student-Alumni Career Connect! Be sure to set … Read More View All Resources Vault Guides Skip filter options to posts Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Resource Categories: Advising Guidelines Applications Career Guides Hiring Policies How-tos & Examples Industry Reports Professional Writing Samples Third Party Resources Vault Guides Close Clear Filters Vault Guide to Networking Share This: Share Vault Guide to Networking on Facebook Share Vault Guide to Networking on LinkedIn Share Vault Guide to Networking on X Copy Link When it comes to job success, it’s not only what you know: it’s who you know. Every year employers fill … Vault #9781438165615 Show author info A comprehensive resource for students and job seekers looking for career advice, job postings, company reviews from employees, and rankings of the best companies and industry employers. facebook instagram linkedin twitter Read More View All Resources Videos How To Do an Informational Interview Video post How To Create Your 30 Second Elevator Pitch! | The Intern Queen Video post Job Fair Advice: How to Use Your 5 Minutes to Get an Interview Video post Opening doors to the American Dream: Robneek and Jill’s Journey with Prudential and Braven Video post View All Videos Alumni Mentors Create a profile, connect with others, and build your network. Click a profile below or head to Student Alumni Career Connect to get started! Valline Whitsett-Hernandez Alumni Copy Link Professional Paralegal & Notary Services PPNS, LLC PeopleGrove #26892812 Meet Valline Gissell Xochimitl Alumni Copy Link Cashier Customer Service Carvel PeopleGrove #20963646 Meet Gissell Erin Sweeney Alumni Copy Link Equal Justice Works Fellow / Attorney Kids in Need of Defense PeopleGrove #3433189 Meet Erin Michael C. Chiusano Alumni Copy Link Wealth Management Analyst Morgan Stanley PeopleGrove #23544003 Meet Michael C. Kevin Masse Alumni Copy Link PeopleGrove #7364245 Meet Kevin Carolina Martinez Alumni Copy Link Choreographer/Dancer self-employed PeopleGrove #1664852 Meet Carolina Benahir Crespo, MPA Alumni Copy Link Bilingual Counselor NEW JERSEY ASSOCIATION ON CORRECTION - NJAC PeopleGrove #22964980 Meet Benahir Daniel Neuspiel Alumni Copy Link Assistant and Associate Professor Albert Einstein College of Medicine PeopleGrove #22122066 Meet Daniel Italo Moreno Alumni Copy Link Area Operations Manager Amazon PeopleGrove #19787625 Meet Italo Babatunde P. Odubekun Alumni Copy Link Vice President & Counsel CleanCapital PeopleGrove #18094131 Meet Babatunde P. Robert Cook Alumni Copy Link N/ A Retired PeopleGrove #17563053 Meet Robert Anthony D’Arelli Alumni Copy Link PeopleGrove #17360708 Meet Anthony View All People Facebook Instagram X (formerly Twitter) runsa@newark.rutgers.edu CARE Team © 2026 Rutgers University - Newark  |  All Rights Reserved Universitywide New Brunswick Camden RBHS MyRutgers Blackboard ScarletMail People Search Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution Privacy Policy | Terms of Service"
