    "https://careers.newark.rutgers.edu/channels/personal-statements/": {
      "title": "Personal Statements",
      "description": "Personal Statements – Career Resources and Exploration | Rutgers University – Newark Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Log in Sign up Guests Search Keywords Make an Appointment Rutgers-Newark Handshake Request a Workshop Home About Us Staff CRE Student Employees Student Outcomes People We Connect Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Campus Partners Faculty Employers/Recruiters Family Industry Pathways Exploring/Multiple Interests Arts, Media, & Entertainment Data & Technology Financial Services, Logistics, & Management Government, Law, & Public Policy Healthcare, Pharmaceuticals, & Sciences Natural Resources, Sustainability, & Environmental Science Nonprofit, Social Justice, & Education Explore Opportunities Detecting Fraudulent Job Postings Experiential Opportunities Jobs and Internships Job Searching Making Connections Rutgers Scarlet Service Internship (RSSI) Program Professional Resources CareerThreads – Free Professional Attire Raider Headshot Studio Majors and Careers Get Career Ready Career Ready in Real Life Resumes and Cover Letters Interviewing Graduate and Professional School Personal Statements Videos on Demand Events All Events Fall 2026 Raider Career and Internship Fair at Rutgers University-Newark Raider Career Impact Awards Personal Statements Latest News Latest News Forage Experiences Career Resources Vault Guides Videos The personal statement is a chance for you to describe how you are the ideal candidate in your own words. Help the reader understand who you are, and why you should be selected for the opportunity. Here are a few suggestions to get started: Answer the question(s). Read the prompt and make sure you are answering the specific question(s) that are being asked. If there is no prompt provided, think about addressing the following: -Interest: What led you to consider this type of program? -Preparation: What have you done to continue exploring your interest? How have you developed the types of skills and/or knowledge that show that you continue to learn more about the field? (Remember that proof of your experiences, not promises of what you will do, are persuasive.) -Motivation: How have you shown that this is an interest that has grown over time? Share your story. Focus on the elements that have helped you to personally decide on this goal. What makes a personal statement stand out is if it is a genuine, personal reflection of interests, preparation, and motivation. Proofread what you have written. Give yourself enough time to create a well-written statement, and then make sure that you have time to review your statement. Spell-check and careful review of your statement are important to show that the words are a reflection of your writing abilities and you as a candidate. Get feedback on your statement. Ask others to read your statement, and share their thoughts. Feedback may help you to discover places you were unclear, or information you’re missing. Sidebar Latest News Reach Your Professional Goals and Build Your Skills…Right from Your Laptop! A Year of Growth | Celebrating What You Achieved in 2020 How I Recruit | A Conversation with Stephen Ostendorff about Grad School Admissions 5 Podcasts to Help You Think (and Talk) About Race Idealist Careers Try This Challenge #1 | Reflect on Your Successes View All Career Resources Tips for Talking to Graduate/Professional School Recruiters Share This: Share Tips for Talking to Graduate/Professional School Recruiters on Facebook Share Tips for Talking to Graduate/Professional School Recruiters on LinkedIn Share Tips for Talking to Graduate/Professional School Recruiters on X Copy Link Potential questions to ask: What are your graduates prepared to do?\nWhat areas do your grads work in?\nAre there … Read More Personal Statements and Application Letters Share This: Share Personal Statements and Application Letters on Facebook Share Personal Statements and Application Letters on LinkedIn Share Personal Statements and Application Letters on X Copy Link View Resource Writing the Personal Statement Share This: Share Writing the Personal Statement on Facebook Share Writing the Personal Statement on LinkedIn Share Writing the Personal Statement on X Copy Link View Resource Pre-Professional Programs Share This: Share Pre-Professional Programs on Facebook Share Pre-Professional Programs on LinkedIn Share Pre-Professional Programs on X Copy Link View Resource Writing Center Share This: Share Writing Center on Facebook Share Writing Center on LinkedIn Share Writing Center on X Copy Link View Resource View All Resources Facebook Instagram X (formerly Twitter) runsa@newark.rutgers.edu CARE Team © 2026 Rutgers University - Newark  |  All Rights Reserved Universitywide New Brunswick Camden RBHS MyRutgers Blackboard ScarletMail People Search Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is an equal opportunity, affirmative action institution Privacy Policy | Terms of Service"
    },
    "https://careers.newark.rutgers.edu/channels/video-resources-and-recorded-events/": {
      "title": "CRE On Demand!",
